V8: "[compiler] Mark JSGetTemplateObject as able to write" (crbug 574339635;
no CVE listed yet): TurboFan treated JSGetTemplateObject as not writing, so
load elimination kept known maps across it and dropped map checks, although
the first evaluation of a tagged template can migrate Array.prototype's map:
memory corruption reachable from page JavaScript. V8 main commit
7e802b909a04cc30207168e42edbd64e4d3d4bf7, merged on 2026-10-30 to V8 15.8,
15.7 (ea8bd7b6ff6a9b494909e1ff3c723a193b86dba3, for 157) and 15.6
(1f76a38270ac0bf61b9d23f2aab85aa9b5795504, for 156). This is the 15.7 merge,
at v8/, without its test. Drop it once a 157 tag's V8 has it.

